# CONTROL for the `ship-intersect-w2x-2m` arm comparison: `continue` at reveal=design.
#
# WHAT IT SEPARATES. In that campaign `meta` runs at reveal=design and the three per-design arms
# (from_scratch / continue / closest) run at reveal=none, so meta's win confounds TWO changes: the
# continual+replay training AND the input representation. Those are not two encodings of one task --
# `address_combine` (5 features: TDC + station/view/layer/straw indices) reports only WHICH straw
# fired and WHEN, while `four_feature_combine` (4 features: TDC, norm z, wire_y_left, wire_y_right)
# resolves the design into each hit's own geometry, and `straw.py:address_combine` states outright
# that the network must otherwise work the geometry out for itself, so losses are NOT comparable
# across the two. This cell makes one per-design arm comparable to meta.
#
# ONE SEED, draw 1 of the campaign generator `random.Random(123456).randint(0, 2**31-1)` =
# 1244111331, so it pairs cell-for-cell with the banked reveal=none `continue` at the same seed.
#
# Its own tree (`-reveal`), NOT a fifth arm inside `ship-intersect-w2x-2m`: the campaign's per-seed
# directory holds exactly the four arm names and a plot over that tree would silently pool a cell
# that is not on the same task as its siblings.
universe       = vanilla
executable     = geom_cell.sh
arguments      = ship_intersect_prec1e2_w2x_2m $(seed) $(arm) $(reveal) /afs/cern.ch/work/m/maborisy/ship-intersect-w2x-2m-reveal/$(seed)/$(arm)
output         = logs/isect2mrev_$(seed)_$(arm).$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).out
error          = logs/isect2mrev_$(seed)_$(arm).$(ClusterId).$(ProcId).err
log            = logs/isect2mrev.$(ClusterId).log
request_gpus   = 1
request_cpus   = 2
request_memory = 12000
requirements   = TARGET.GPUs_GlobalMemoryMb >= 20000
+MaxRuntime    = 172800
+JobBatchName  = "ship-intersect-w2x-2m-reveal"
queue seed,arm,reveal from (
  1244111331, continue, design
)
